# pnpm keeps a strict, isolated node_modules: only direct dependencies are
# linked at the project root. ESLint's flat config resolves plugins from the
# project root, but `eslint-config-next` pulls its plugins in transitively
# (@next/eslint-plugin-next, eslint-plugin-react-hooks, react, import-x, …).
# They end up in the store but not at the root, so every lint run — including
# the one `next build` performs — died with "couldn't find the plugin".
#
# The build did not fail, which is why this went unnoticed: Next logs the
# ESLint failure and carries on, so lint has effectively not been running at
# all, locally or on Netlify.
#
# Hoisting just the eslint packages fixes resolution without giving up pnpm's
# isolation for everything else (which `shamefully-hoist` would).
public-hoist-pattern[]=*eslint*
public-hoist-pattern[]=@next/eslint-plugin-next
